\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 Eloise Shakti, CEO
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \'93Good morning Eloise.\'94 Sarah greeted on the other end of the vid-phone. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes, how can I help you?\'94 Eloise said. \'93As I am a very busy person these days.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I wish to arranged a meeting with you today.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93In regards to what?\'94 Eloise asked.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93The cyber attack upon the financial system of the PTD.\'94 Sarah replied.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I think we have that matter under control.\'94 Although Eloise was yet to hear from the two privateers she had set upon Cracker she was unconcerned. Wet work of mercenaries could not be hurried or managed with timetables or measured on a clock. These things took as long as they took. She was confident that the level 2 dullard known as Cracker would sell-out all of the Elvi in an instant to save his worthless hide. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I would insist we speak.\'94 Sarah pressed, then after some thought added, \'93Richard would very much like to see you, too.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Oh, why didn\'92t you say?\'94 Eloise voice immediately changed to a bright friendly, pleasant tone. \'93I always have time for my grandson. I have no meetings between 3 and 4pm today. See you both then.\'94 She terminated the communication.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0  - - -
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 As the meeting with Sarah approached, Eloise still had not heard from her operatives and she was now reasonably sure the mission had failed. Sarah\'92s overtures for an impromptu family reunion had become increasingly suspicious as the time passed and no word was received. Sarah must about the raid, that much was certain. Machiavellian by choice, Eloise was always prepared for setbacks and had an infinite capacity for thinking on her feet and taking the most aggressive option available. No matter what Sarah had to say, Eloise would have an answer. If that failed, extortion was not beneath her.
\f1 \

\f2  
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Thank you for making the time for Richard and I, Eloise.\'94 Sarah said placing Richard on the floor. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Come here my little marvel.\'94 Eloise bent down, arms out, awaiting the familiar crash of Richard gleefully running into her embrace, but Richard remained stationary, a look of disdain across his little face. \'93What\'92s wrong, little man?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You tried to kill, Cracker. Grandmother.\'94 Richard said slowly.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93What?\'94 Eloise was in shock. \'93He speaks!\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes, I do Grand-mama.\'94 Richard confirmed.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93And with an English accent, no less!\'94 Eliose replied. \'93Received pronunciation accent, it is not?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'91Yes, grand-mama.\'94 Richard said, \'93It is not by choice. This body speaks this way.\'94\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93We are here to discuss why you would send goons to rough up, Cracker.\'94 Sarah interjected. As interesting as she found the discussion, she thought they should get to the business at hand. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Oh, Sarah, my daughter-in-law, why do you care for the fate of such a low-life?\'94 Eloise was genuinely perplexed. \'93He is nothing, an uneducated orphan with no prospects.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93He is the only living beneficiary to the Hardy fortune.\'94 Sarah countered. \'93He will be the richest person who ever lived. Doesn\'92t that count as prospects?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Bah! Any claim to the Hardy fortune will be blocked in the courts and I will ensure he is stuck in litigation for years, decades if necessary. He will never inherit anything.\'94 Eloise decreed. \'93N.O.O.C. darling - Not of our class. He will not inherit credit one.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Grand-mama, you are wrong.\'94 Richard countered.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Well it seems we are going to have to teach you some manners, young man.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93No, you must learn.\'94 Richard eyes met with Eloise. \'93Class structures do not promote the evolution of the individual, it crushes the majority for the benefit of the few.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Oh dear! A lib-tard lefty!\'94 Eloise rolled her eyes, genuinely frustrated. \'93You have a lot a growing up to do.\'94 She laughed, just a little, at the picture of her telling a toddler he has a lot of growing up to do. \'93Sarah? What have you been teaching my grandson?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I learn myself.\'94 Richard protests.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93We are not here for a debate on the merits of our social structures.\'94 Sarah again tried to get the conversation back on track. \'93What did you think you were doing sending those men to obtain access to the Hardy finance data base.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Simple, my dear.\'94 Eloise smiled widely. \'93I wish to take control of the system for the benefit of the PTD.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Altruism from you?\'94 Sarah giggled at the absurdity. 
\f3\i Eloise-the-atruistic\cf2 ? 
\f2\i0 \cf0 \'93I think you may have your own welfare in mind.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Of course\'94 Eloise admitted. \'93Benevolence gets you nowhere, you know that. It is just that I cannot allow that Cracker person to have access to such an important and dangerous resource.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93It is not your property and it is not up to you.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93The existence of Jamison Hardy\'92s finance system is a clear and present danger to the financial health of our Dominion. I am the CEO and the PTD has suffered an attack. I cannot allow a repeat.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You personally benefited from the \'91attack\'92 as you call it.\'94 Sarah pointed out. \'93I did not have to let you in on it. You could have suffered like the rest, but I did not let that happen.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Had you not, dear, this conversation would have been very different.\'94 Eloise warned.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I figured that, but it was my expectation you would display something similar to gratitude.\'94 Sarah replied. \'93It does not seem unreasonable.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I decide what is reasonable!\'94 Eloise raised her voice, her eyes wide and wild. \'93I am the CEO, I decide what will and what will not happen in the PTD. You may have your expectations, but I have my duty and I must protect the economic interest of the dominion. Family, friends and old associations are secondary considerations.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Thank you, Grand-mama.\'94 Richard interrupted. \'93I think mother will agree that there is now no chance of you being granted access.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Is that right, my little grandson?\'94 Eloise smiled, turning to Sarah she continued, \'93Some disturbing information has crossed my desk over the past few days. It would seem our illustrious Police Commissioner is also a revered religious figure of the Elvi Nation. A religious figure! And it is suspected she has acted against the interests of the PTD, on behalf of the Elvi.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Don\'92t be ridiculous.\'94 Sarah replied. \'93As sad as it is, she\'92s 100% cop.\'94
\f1 \

\f2  
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Mind your words young lady.\'94 Eloise warned Sarah for the second time. \'93There are rumours spreading that not only was she behind the Black Monday cyber-attack, she has a clandestine operation underway on the outskirts of town. Some say she is cooking up a weapon of some sort.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You know she wasn\'92t behind the cyber attack and I understand police operations are sometimes clandestine.\'94 Sarah was a little rattled, security around the operation is water tight\'85..oh shit, Shakti! 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Details like that do not matter.\'94 Eloise volleyed back.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Details? Like the truth?\'94 Sarah incredulous.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93The truth is always a matter of perspective and my truth has the backing of the PTD.\'94 Eloise replied. \'93The Board of Directors will take the view that she was either involved or she allowed it to happen due to incompetence. Either way, her position as Commissioner is shaky at best.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93You cannot afford to lose such a dedicated officer!\'94 Sarah pleaded in high voice. 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Dedicated?\'94 Eloise face screwed-up. \'93Was it dedication on display when she took the title of Holy Aunt Hayley?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93The Elvi call me Blessed Mother. It means nothing apart from, perhaps, respect.\'94 Sarah explained. \'93I did not, nor did Hayley, ask for respect or reverence from the Elvi. Quite the opposite in fact.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93It matters not. Hayley cannot be both Commissioner and Holy Icon and since she has not control over whether she is a Holy Icon,, she cannot be the Commissioner.\'94 Eloise said. \'93I will be asking for her resignation and if that is not forthcoming her contract will be terminated, along with her.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93That is evil.\'94 Richard said quietly.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Or I can be granted access to the system.\'94 Eloise said, smile radiating white.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93I will speak with Hayley and get back to you.\'94 Sarah said, her eye unable to meet Eloise\'92s gaze.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Good. I expect an answer by the end of the week.\'94 Eloise said at speed. \'93Now, Richard are you going to give Grand-mama a hug?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes.\'94 Richard hugged her as hard he could and with his mouth to her ear whispered, \'93Please don\'92t hurt my friends Grand-mama. I need them for what is to come.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \'93It\'92s just business, Richard. You will understand when you are older.\'94 Eloise lifted Richard to the waiting arms of Sarah.
\f1 \

\f2 \'93This is a terrible business.\'94 Sarah terminated the conversation and took Richard out the door.
\f1 \
